  "result": "Perfect! All 171 tests pass. Let me verify the complete implementation:\n\n**Summary of date utilities:**\n\n1. **src/dates.js** \u2014 Created three utility functions:\n   - `isValidDate(text)`: Validates YYYY-MM-DD format and checks if the date exists\n     - Rejects non-strings, invalid formats, invalid dates (Feb 30, etc.)\n     - Accepts valid leap years (Feb 29 in leap years)\n     - All arithmetic in UTC\n   \n   - `addDays(date, n)`: Adds n days to a date string\n     - Returns new date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n     - Handles positive and negative days\n     - Correctly crosses month/year boundaries\n     - Uses UTC arithmetic\n   \n   - `daysBetween(a, b)`: Calculates whole days between two dates (b minus a)\n     - Returns integer number of days\n     - Returns 0 for same date\n     - Returns negative for reversed dates\n     - Uses UTC arithmetic\n\n2. **Updated createInvoice** in src/invoices.js:\n   - Removed old `validateDate` function\n   - Now uses `isValidDate` from dates module\n   - Maintains same validation behavior\n\n3. **Comprehensive test suite** \u2014 23 new tests covering:\n   - Valid/invalid date formats and values\n   - Leap year handling\n   - Month and year boundary crossing\n   - Negative day operations\n   - Inverse relationship between `addDays` and `daysBetween`\n   - Multi-year calculations\n   - Non-string input rejection\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- All dates are 'YYYY-MM-DD' strings throughout the system\n- All arithmetic uses UTC (T00:00:00Z) to avoid timezone issues\n- `daysBetween` uses whole days (Math.floor), not fractional\n- Functions are timezone-agnostic and deterministic",
